  "computed_vs_declared_resonance": {
    "f_resonant_computed_hz": 32487.4,
    "f_resonant_declared_hz": 25000.0,
    "f_switching_nominal_hz": 35000.0,
    "finding": "main.ato:74 declares f_resonant_nominal=25kHz, implying a 10kHz design margin below the 35kHz nominal switching frequency (main.ato:71). Computed from the ACTUAL committed tank capacitance (300nF, modules.ato c_tank1+c_tank2) and the coil inductance pan_load.sub assumes (80uH, itself uncalibrated -- see above), the tank's own resonance is 32487Hz -- leaving only 2513Hz of margin above resonance at nominal switching frequency, not 10kHz. This sweep's own grid results (below) show that margin collapsing completely by 32kHz, i.e. within ~9% of the nominal 35kHz switching frequency -- much closer to the edge than the design's own stated intent assumes, if the coil ends up anywhere near pan_load.sub's assumed 80uH."
  },
